      "degradation": {
        "review_status": "needs_review",
        "ownerApproved": false,
        "promotionAuthorized": false,
        "method": "Replace concrete obligations, decisions, and consequences with wellness and capacity abstractions. Leave heading, date range, astrology, attribution, key dates, paragraph count, and all other prose byte-identical.",
        "replacements": [
          {
            "paragraphIndex": 2,
            "sourceSha256": "fab2f81e66891cef0b5fe316a37bf9513157952cd315e721be315b7742b211f7",
            "replacement": "The change may be something you choose, or the old setup may simply stop being workable. Your capacity, alignment, needs, and evolving priorities may ask you to honor what fits now instead of what fit before."
          },
          {
            "paragraphIndex": 3,
            "sourceSha256": "0f1973f9e6a13ca08090ed04065ba8a3a82274d656863ec770f898068c2fc152",
            "replacement": "You may need to honor your capacity, protect your energy, create more space, or choose terms that support your well-being. You may step back from what no longer feels sustainable. You may change how you relate to the opportunity or release what requires you to remain unchanged."
          },
          {
            "paragraphIndex": 6,
            "sourceSha256": "5976ed2dbbee04f214512fcb2e031dabd45e4beb0cb3e53ae2d5e30cd6b76346",
            "replacement": "This can show up in relationships too. A connection may need to reflect your current capacity and the person you are becoming. The relationship may ask for more alignment, more spaciousness, or a healthier balance between your needs and the needs of others. Different terms may help everyone honor the changes already taking place."
          },
          {
            "paragraphIndex": 10,
            "sourceSha256": "dc2305f8b66712de4041ac5347bb415b9a49d5fb7835788f45fc38988354eb3d",
            "replacement": "This matters if you are looking for work too. An opportunity may appear aligned while the conditions around it ask you to compromise your capacity or well-being. The process can clarify what supports your growth and what you are no longer available to carry."
          },
          {
            "paragraphIndex": 11,
            "sourceSha256": "f4a3babbf6e15b7445f5c10f7688c195bc45a65698c1084512835b670ca39662",
            "replacement": "The same logic applies outside work. A connection or collaboration may look supportive until the energetic exchange reveals that the balance is no longer sustainable."
          }
        ]
      },
